{
  "dom_id": "questionExplanation-16262",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "As $x$ approaches $1,$ the value of $f(x)$ approaches $3.$ Consequently, \n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to \\,1}f(x)=3\\,.\n$$\n\nRemember, it does not matter that the actual value of $f(1)$ is $2.$ All that matters is that as $x$ approaches $1,$ the function $f(x)$ *looks like* it is getting closer and closer to $3.$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
